---
import { TEMPLATE_CATALOG } from '@/data/template-catalog'

const baseline = [
  { title: 'A consistent codebase', tool: 'Biome', body: 'Linting and formatting rules live in the repo, so everyone works from the same standard.' },
  { title: 'Types that have your back', tool: 'TypeScript', body: 'Strict type checking makes mistakes visible while you’re building, before they reach a review.' },
  { title: 'Checks that travel with you', tool: 'GitHub Actions', body: 'Run your project’s checks in CI, with editor settings and agent guidance alongside them.' },
]
---

<div class="xt-home">
  <div class="xt-home-ecosystem">
    <p>Good tools.<br /><strong>Already working together.</strong></p>
    <ul aria-label="Tools in the shared baseline"><li>Biome</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>GitHub Actions</li><li>VS Code</li><li>Agent skills</li></ul>
  </div>

  <section class="xt-home-section" aria-labelledby="two-tools">
    <div class="xt-home-section-heading">
      <h2 id="two-tools">A fresh start.<br />Or a better foundation.</h2>
      <p>Two tools for wherever you are in your project. One shared baseline for what comes next.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xt-home-paths">
      <article class="xt-home-path">
        <div class="xt-home-path-symbol" aria-hidden="true">+</div>
        <p class="xt-home-path-context">For your next project</p>
        <h3>Skip the setup.<br />Keep the possibilities.</h3>
        <p>Pick a Next.js or Vite + React template. Start with linting, strict types, CI, and editor settings in place.</p>
        <div class="xt-home-command"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span><code>pnpm create xtarter-app@latest</code></div>
        <a class="xt-home-text-link" href="/create-xtarter-app/" data-umami-event="tool_card_click" data-umami-event-product="create-xtarter-app">Explore create-xtarter-app <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="xt-home-path">
        <div class="xt-home-path-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
        <p class="xt-home-path-context">For the repo you already have</p>
        <h3>Your project.<br />Up to your standards.</h3>
        <p>Let xtarterize detect your stack and plan the configuration changes. Review the plan, then approve what gets applied.</p>
        <div class="xt-home-command"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span><code>pnpx xtarterize@latest init</code></div>
        <a class="xt-home-text-link" href="/xtarterize/" data-umami-event="tool_card_click" data-umami-event-product="xtarterize">Explore xtarterize <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="xt-home-command-note">Prefer npm, Yarn, or Bun? The getting-started guides include commands for your package manager.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-home-section xt-home-baseline-section" aria-labelledby="the-baseline">
    <div class="xt-home-section-heading">
      <h2 id="the-baseline">The details you’d set up anyway.<br />Ready from the start.</h2>
      <a class="xt-home-text-link" href="/xtarterize/guide/tasks/overview/">See the conformance tasks <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a>
    </div>
    <ul class="xt-home-benefits">
      {baseline.map((item) => (
        <li><span class="xt-home-tool-label">{item.tool}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.body}</p></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="xt-home-safety">
      <div><h3>Make changes with confidence.</h3><p>xtarterize previews the plan, surfaces conflicts, and backs up modified files. Undo and restore are built in.</p></div>
      <a class="xt-home-text-link" href="/xtarterize/guide/cli/overview/">Read how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-home-section" aria-labelledby="starter-templates">
    <div class="xt-home-section-heading">
      <h2 id="starter-templates">Find your starting point.</h2>
      <p>Five curated templates. Familiar frameworks, your choice of UI, and a baseline you can build on.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="xt-home-templates">
      {TEMPLATE_CATALOG.map((template) => (
        <li><a href={`https://github.com/${template.repo}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-umami-event="template_click" data-umami-event-template_name={template.name}>
          <span class="xt-home-template-icon" aria-hidden="true">{template.id.startsWith('next') ? 'N' : 'V'}</span>
          <span class="xt-home-template-copy"><span class="xt-home-template-name">{template.name}</span><span class="xt-home-template-description">{template.description}</span></span>
          <span class="xt-home-template-stack">{template.stack.find((part) => /Chakra|Tailwind|Hero/.test(part))}</span>
          <span class="xt-home-template-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span>
        </a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="xt-home-template-footer"><p>Choose a template. Make it yours.</p><a class="xt-home-text-link" href="/create-xtarter-app/guide/templates/">Compare the templates <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-home-closing" aria-labelledby="get-started">
    <div><h2 id="get-started">Your next idea starts here.</h2><p>Get the foundation in place. Then get back to building.</p></div>
    <div class="xt-home-actions"><a class="xt-home-button" href="/create-xtarter-app/getting-started/" data-umami-event="band_cta_browse">Start a new project</a><a class="xt-home-button xt-home-button-secondary" href="/xtarterize/getting-started/" data-umami-event="band_cta_conform">Improve an existing repo</a></div>
  </section>

  <footer class="xt-home-footer">
    <a class="xt-home-footer-brand" href="/">xtarter<span>Less setup. More building.</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Project information"><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarterize">GitHub</a></nav>
  </footer>
</div>
